---
// The research page collects preprints, theses, and other writings.
import ThemeInit from "../components/ThemeInit.astro";
import SiteNav from "../components/SiteNav.astro";
import PageWatermark from "../components/PageWatermark.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin="anonymous" />
    <link rel="preload" as="image" href="/Chow%20quotient.jpg" />
    <link
      rel="stylesheet"
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;0,600;0,650;0,700;1,400&amp;family=STIX+Two+Text:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;0,700;1,400&amp;display=swap"
    />
    <ThemeInit />
    <title>Research | Suraj Dash</title>
  </head>
  <body class="research-page">
    <PageWatermark src="/Chow%20quotient.jpg" />
    <main class="page-shell">
      <SiteNav current="/research" />

    

      <section class="research-layout" aria-label="Research overview">
        <div class="publications">
          <article class="publication-card research-articles" aria-labelledby="research-articles-heading">
            <h2 id="research-articles-heading">Research articles</h2>
            <ul class="research-article-list">
              <li class="research-article">
                <div class="publication-heading">
                  <button class="research-article-toggle" id="git-title" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="git-description">
                    <span class="research-arrow" aria-hidden="true">▶</span>
                    <span class="publication-title">Variation of GIT for Hilbert Schemes of Expansions.</span>
                  </button>
                  <span class="publication-status">(Draft available)</span>
                </div>
                <div class="research-description" id="git-description" role="region" aria-labelledby="git-title" aria-hidden="true" inert>
                  <div class="research-description-clip">
                    <div class="research-description-layout">
                    <div class="research-description-content">
                      <p>
                        For a smooth projective variety <math class="inline-math" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" aria-label="X"><mi>X</mi></math> with normal crossings boundary <math class="inline-math" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" aria-label="D"><mi>D</mi></math>,
                        compactifying <math class="inline-math" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" aria-label="Hilbert scheme of n points on X minus D"><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Hilb</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></math> requires understanding limits of
                        subschemes approaching <math class="inline-math" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" aria-label="D"><mi>D</mi></math>. Ordinary flat limits may acquire support on
                        <math class="inline-math" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" aria-label="D"><mi>D</mi></math>, or on the singular locus when the target degenerates. The expanded
                        constructions of Li and Li–Wu insert additional components into the target
                        to accommodate such limits. Logarithmic Hilbert spaces
                        then impose a transversality condition, requiring the support of limiting
                        subschemes to avoid the boundary and singular locus of the expanded fibre.
                      </p>
                      <p id="git-coarse-paragraph">
                        In this project, we ask how relaxing this transversality condition changes the
                        compactification. Building on the GIT construction of
                        Gulbrandsen–Halle–Hulek, we study the full relative Hilbert
                        scheme of an expansion and vary stability using its natural torus action.
                        Different stability conditions allow different boundary configurations,
                        with transitions occurring along walls in the parameter space. We classify
                        the configurations responsible for these walls and the resulting birational
                        transformations, providing a systematic way to compare the corresponding
                        compactifications and their geometric invariants.
                      </p>
                      <button class="diagram-toggle" id="git-coarse-diagram-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="git-coarse-diagram">
                        <math class="inline-math" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" aria-label="LogHilb squared of the projective line with infinity"><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">LogHilb</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>∞</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow></math>
                        <span class="diagram-map-target"><svg class="diagram-map-arrow" viewBox="0 0 32 12" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M2 6H26" stroke-dasharray=".1 3" stroke-linecap="round" /><path d="m23 2 5 4-5 4" /></svg><math class="inline-math" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" aria-label="maps to Hilb squared of the projective line"><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Hilb</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></math></span>
                        <span class="diagram-toggle-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
                      </button>
                      <p id="git-toric-paragraph">
                        We use invariant divisorial valuations, inspired by Altmann–Hausen, to encode the support walls for expanded SNC pairs; for pointed curves, the additional discriminant walls sensitive to the scheme structure exhaust the full equivariant ample cone. This gives an explicit VGIT path from <math class="inline-math" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" aria-label="LogHilb"><mi mathvariant="normal">LogHilb</mi></math> to <math class="inline-math" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" aria-label="Hilb"><mi mathvariant="normal">Hilb</mi></math>. We use these wall-crossings to compute the integral Chow ring of <math class="inline-math" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" aria-label="LogHilb"><mi mathvariant="normal">LogHilb</mi></math> and, in genus zero, study its Mori geometry.
                      </p>
                      <button class="diagram-toggle" id="git-toric-diagram-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="git-toric-diagram">
                        <span>Toric</span>
                        <math class="inline-math" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" aria-label="LogHilb squared of the projective line with infinity"><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">LogHilb</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>∞</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow></math>
                        <span class="diagram-toggle-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
                      </button>
                      <p>
                        For surfaces, new wall crossings appear already in length two, including a Francia flip. For <math class="inline-math" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" aria-label="the projective plane with a line"><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℙ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mtext>line</mtext><mo>)</mo></mrow></math>, this wall-crossing computes the integral Chow ring, recovering Setayesh’s rational result obtained by torus localization. I am currently working on extending these methods to general toric pairs.
                      </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="diagram-panels" id="git-diagrams" hidden>
                    <aside class="diagram-panel" id="git-coarse-diagram" aria-labelledby="git-coarse-diagram-title" hidden>
                      <div class="diagram-panel-heading">
                        <h3 class="diagram-map-title" id="git-coarse-diagram-title"><math class="inline-math" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" aria-label="LogHilb squared of the projective line with infinity"><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">LogHilb</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>∞</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow></math><span class="diagram-map-target"><svg class="diagram-map-arrow" viewBox="0 0 32 12" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M2 6H26" stroke-dasharray=".1 3" stroke-linecap="round" /><path d="m23 2 5 4-5 4" /></svg><math class="inline-math" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" aria-label="maps to Hilb squared of the projective line"><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Hilb</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></math></span></h3>
                        <button class="diagram-close" type="button" aria-label="Close LogHilb diagram">×</button>
                      </div>
                      <a class="diagram-image-link" href="/diagrams/loghilb2-p1-coarse.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the LogHilb diagram at full size in a new tab">
                        <img src="/diagrams/loghilb2-p1-coarse.svg" width="1502" height="889" alt="Coarse LogHilb²(ℙ¹, D) over the chart U, mapping by the blow-up of (x², y) to U = 𝔸² inside Hilb²(ℙ¹) = ℙ². The coarse space and the dotted neighbourhood U are filled sky blue; the exceptional curve E is red and the discriminant Δ is green." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                      </a>
                      <p class="diagram-caption">Select the diagram to view full size.</p>
                    </aside>
                    <aside class="diagram-panel" id="git-toric-diagram" aria-labelledby="git-toric-diagram-title" hidden>
                      <div class="diagram-panel-heading">
                        <h3 id="git-toric-diagram-title">Toric <math class="inline-math" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" aria-label="LogHilb squared of the projective line with infinity"><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">LogHilb</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>∞</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow></math></h3>
                        <button class="diagram-close" type="button" aria-label="Close toric LogHilb diagram">×</button>
                      </div>
                      <a class="diagram-image-link" href="/diagrams/loghilb2-p1-toric.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open the toric LogHilb diagram at full size in a new tab">
                        <img src="/diagrams/loghilb2-p1-toric.svg" width="2000" height="687" alt="Toric diagram showing successive subdivisions of the triangular sector from Σ for ℙ³ to Σ₃,₃ and then Σ for Q₀, with w₃ = 3v₀ + 2v₁ + v₂ and w₂ = 2v₀ + v₁; the polyhedral diagram on the right has labelled vertices v₀, v₁, v₂, v₃, w₃ and w₂." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                      </a>
                      <p class="diagram-caption">Select the diagram to view full size.</p>
                    </aside>
                    </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li class="research-article">
                <div class="publication-heading">
                  <button class="research-article-toggle" id="stability-title" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="stability-description">
                    <span class="research-arrow" aria-hidden="true">▶</span>
                    <span class="publication-title">K-stability of singular del Pezzo surfaces.</span>
                  </button>
                  <span class="publication-status">(In preparation)</span>
                </div>
                <p class="publication-collaborators">
                  With Kristin DeVleming, Fernando Figueroa, Gomathy Ganapathy, Myeong Jae Jeon, Tyson Klingner, Daniel Mallory, and Ying Wang.
                </p>
                <div class="research-description" id="stability-description" role="region" aria-labelledby="stability-title" aria-hidden="true" inert>
                  <div class="research-description-clip">
                    <!-- Project description can be added here. -->
                  </div>
                </div>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </article>

         

          <article class="publication-card">
            <h2>Theses</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>
                <div class="publication-heading">
                  <span class="publication-title"><strong>PhD thesis:</strong> Variation of GIT for Hilbert Schemes of Expansions.</span>
                  <span class="publication-status">(In progress, expected 2027)</span>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Master’s thesis:</strong>
                Logarithmic construction of the moduli space of admissible covers
                (<a href="http://tesi.cab.unipd.it/65771" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Thesis</a>).
              </li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <article class="publication-card">
            <h2>Other writings</h2>
            <p class="writing-disclaimer">
              These notes record my personal understanding of the material, based on the references cited in the bibliography. They are intended as expository notes and contain no claim of original mathematical contribution. Despite my efforts to present the material accurately, the notes may contain errors, omissions, or imprecise statements. Any such shortcomings are entirely my own.
            </p>
            <ul>
              <li>Atiyah Flops, Francia Flips and affine VGIT (<a href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1uRc5zzbQF0ub1pYbfLoxu6bYeqD7tRZ8/view?usp=sharing" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Notes</a>).</li>
              <li>Logarithmic geometry (<a href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1KLB7g7ZqgS8oFNCY-9ohfsGLNoHs4VUS/view?usp=sharing" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Notes</a>).</li>
              <li>
                A gentle introduction to the Virtual Fundamental Class (<a href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1UpmtpUzZpdNmcOS9rjRq_MHhE7mxCwRg/view?usp=sharing" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Notes</a>).
                <span class="writing-context">Notes for Junior QFT seminar, UT Austin</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                Moduli of ASD connections and Donaldson invariants (<a href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VxpPCmAxMw0Mhz713AYsUZs-Dhr58TSG/view?usp=sharing" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Notes</a>).
                <span class="writing-context">Moduli in geometry seminar, UT Austin</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                Fourier-Mukai transforms and the Bondal-Orlov theorem (<a href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1v8IMqeVE-YUdGptCrw7LcHzx0oalnBno/view?usp=sharing" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Notes</a>).
                <span class="writing-context">Notes for Kylerec workshop, 2023</span>
              </li>
              <li>
                A gentle introduction to Bridgeland stability (<a href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1qOawaoNksvFa5f6yE2KrGydsgE00kmTg/view?usp=sharing" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Notes</a>).
                <span class="writing-context">Notes for literature seminar, UT Austin</span>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <p class="background-caption">
        Watermark: Chow quotient of <span class="caption-math">LogHilb<sup>2</sup>(ℙ<sup>1</sup>, ∞)</span>.
      </p>
      <SiteFooter />
    </main>
  </body>
</html>

<script>
  const researchCard = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>(".research-articles");
  const researchToggles = Array.from(
    researchCard?.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>(".research-article-toggle") ?? []
  );
  const diagramToggles = Array.from(
    researchCard?.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>(".diagram-toggle") ?? []
  );
  const diagramPanels = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#git-diagrams");
  const descriptionContent = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#git-description .research-description-content");
  const coarseParagraph = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#git-coarse-paragraph");
  const toricParagraph = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#git-toric-paragraph");
  const coarsePanel = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#git-coarse-diagram");
  const toricPanel = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#git-toric-diagram");
  let openDiagramOrder: HTMLButtonElement[] = [];
  let alignmentFrame = 0;

  function alignDiagramPanels() {
    if (!diagramPanels || !coarseParagraph || !toricParagraph || !coarsePanel || !toricPanel) return;
    if (diagramPanels.hidden || !window.matchMedia("(min-width: 1100px)").matches) {
      coarsePanel.style.marginTop = "";
      toricPanel.style.marginTop = "";
      return;
    }
    const columnTop = diagramPanels.getBoundingClientRect().top;
    const gap = parseFloat(getComputedStyle(diagramPanels).rowGap) || 0;
    const coarseOffset = coarsePanel.hidden ? 0 : Math.max(0, coarseParagraph.getBoundingClientRect().top - columnTop);
    const coarseMargin = coarsePanel.hidden ? "" : `${coarseOffset}px`;
    if (coarsePanel.style.marginTop !== coarseMargin) coarsePanel.style.marginTop = coarseMargin;
    const precedingHeight = coarsePanel.hidden ? 0 : coarseOffset + coarsePanel.getBoundingClientRect().height + gap;
    const paragraphTop = toricParagraph.getBoundingClientRect().top;
    const marginTop = toricPanel.hidden ? "" : `${Math.max(0, paragraphTop - columnTop - precedingHeight)}px`;
    if (toricPanel.style.marginTop !== marginTop) toricPanel.style.marginTop = marginTop;
  }

  function scheduleDiagramAlignment() {
    if (alignmentFrame) return;
    alignmentFrame = requestAnimationFrame(() => {
      alignmentFrame = 0;
      alignDiagramPanels();
    });
  }

  const diagramResizeObserver = new ResizeObserver(scheduleDiagramAlignment);
  if (descriptionContent) {
    diagramResizeObserver.observe(descriptionContent);
    descriptionContent.querySelectorAll("p").forEach((paragraph) => diagramResizeObserver.observe(paragraph));
  }
  if (coarsePanel) diagramResizeObserver.observe(coarsePanel);
  window.addEventListener("resize", scheduleDiagramAlignment);

  function setDiagramOpen(toggle: HTMLButtonElement, open: boolean, restoreFocus = false) {
    const panelId = toggle.getAttribute("aria-controls");
    const panel = panelId ? document.getElementById(panelId) : null;
    if (!panel || !diagramPanels || !researchCard) return;
    toggle.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(open));
    panel.hidden = !open;
    openDiagramOrder = openDiagramOrder.filter((other) => other !== toggle);
    if (open) openDiagramOrder.push(toggle);
    const anyOpen = openDiagramOrder.length > 0;
    diagramPanels.hidden = !anyOpen;
    researchCard.dataset.diagramOpen = String(anyOpen);
    alignDiagramPanels();
    if (open) {
      requestAnimationFrame(() => {
        alignDiagramPanels();
        if (!panel.hidden) panel.scrollIntoView({ block: "nearest" });
      });
    }
    if (restoreFocus) toggle.focus();
  }

  diagramToggles.forEach((toggle) => {
    toggle.addEventListener("click", () => {
      setDiagramOpen(toggle, toggle.getAttribute("aria-expanded") !== "true");
    });
    const panelId = toggle.getAttribute("aria-controls");
    const panel = panelId ? document.getElementById(panelId) : null;
    panel?.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(".diagram-close")?.addEventListener("click", () => {
      setDiagramOpen(toggle, false, true);
    });
  });

  function setDescriptionOpen(toggle: HTMLButtonElement, open: boolean) {
    const article = toggle.closest<HTMLElement>(".research-article");
    const description = article?.querySelector<HTMLElement>(".research-description");
    if (!article || !description) return;

    if (!open && toggle.id === "git-title") {
      diagramToggles.forEach((diagramToggle) => setDiagramOpen(diagramToggle, false));
    }

    toggle.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(open));
    article.dataset.expanded = String(open);
    description.setAttribute("aria-hidden", String(!open));
    description.inert = !open;
  }

  researchToggles.forEach((toggle) => {
    toggle.addEventListener("click", () => {
      const shouldOpen = toggle.getAttribute("aria-expanded") !== "true";
      researchToggles.forEach((other) => setDescriptionOpen(other, other === toggle && shouldOpen));
    });
  });

  researchCard?.addEventListener("keydown", (event) => {
    if (event.key !== "Escape") return;
    if (openDiagramOrder.length > 0) {
      const target = event.target instanceof Element ? event.target : null;
      const focusedPanel = target?.closest<HTMLElement>(".diagram-panel");
      const focusedToggle = target?.closest<HTMLButtonElement>(".diagram-toggle");
      const diagramToggle = openDiagramOrder.find((toggle) =>
        toggle === focusedToggle || toggle.getAttribute("aria-controls") === focusedPanel?.id
      ) ?? openDiagramOrder[openDiagramOrder.length - 1];
      setDiagramOpen(diagramToggle, false, true);
      event.preventDefault();
      return;
    }
    const openToggle = researchToggles.find((toggle) => toggle.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true");
    if (!openToggle) return;
    setDescriptionOpen(openToggle, false);
    openToggle.focus();
    event.preventDefault();
  });
</script>

<style>
  :global(:root) {
    --bg: #dfeaf0;
    --surface: #fffaf2;
    --text: #24313a;
    --heading: #304957;
    --muted: #4d606c;
    --accent: #98403a;
    --link: #286784;
    --line: rgba(43, 68, 82, 0.22);
    --card-edge: rgba(49, 98, 118, 0.42);
    --body-glow: rgba(58, 103, 127, 0.1);
    --shadow: rgba(36, 49, 58, 0.09);
    --background-overlay-start: rgba(223, 234, 240, 0.50);
    --background-overlay-end: rgba(223, 234, 240, 0.60);
    --card-bg: rgba(252, 250, 246, 0.90);
    --caption: #405661;
    --caption-shadow: rgba(252, 250, 246, 0.85);
  }

  :global(*) { box-sizing: border-box; }
  :global(body) {
    position: relative;
    isolation: isolate;
    margin: 0;
    min-height: 100vh;
    font-family: "DM Sans", system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
    font-size: 18px;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text);
    background: radial-gradient(circle at top right, var(--body-glow), transparent 34rem), var(--bg);
    transition: color 180ms ease, background-color 180ms ease;
  }
  :global(.page-watermark) { z-index: -1; }
  :global(p) { color: var(--text); line-height: 1.6; }
  :global(a) { color: var(--link); text-decoration-thickness: .08em; text-underline-offset: .16em; }
  .research-layout :global(a) { font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }
  .research-layout :global(a:hover), .research-layout :global(a:focus-visible) { text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-thickness: .1em; text-underline-offset: .18em; }
  :global(strong) { font-weight: 650; }
  h2 { font-family: "DM Sans", system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif; font-weight: 600; color: var(--heading); }
  .page-shell { position: relative; z-index: 1; width: min(1100px, calc(100% - 48px)); min-height: 100vh; margin: 0 auto; padding: 32px 0 112px; }

  .research-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 32px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .publications { display: grid; gap: 18px; max-width: 820px; }

  .publication-card {
    position: relative;
    padding: 22px 24px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 20px;
    background: var(--card-bg);
    box-shadow: 0 14px 36px var(--shadow);
  }

  .publication-card::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: 18px;
    bottom: 18px;
    left: 0;
    width: 3px;
    border-radius: 0 999px 999px 0;
    background: var(--card-edge);
    box-shadow: 1px 0 8px var(--card-edge);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .publication-card h2 {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--heading);
  }

  .publication-card ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
    color: var(--text);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .publication-card li { padding-left: 4px; }

  .publication-heading {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.25rem 0.45rem;
  }

  .publication-title { min-width: 0; }

  .publication-status {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    font-family: "STIX Two Text", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: #925c45;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  :global(html[data-theme="dark"]) .publication-status {
    color: #d6a387;
  }


  .research-articles {
    --description-accent: #925c45;
    --description-bg: rgba(146, 92, 69, 0.055);
  }

  :global(html[data-theme="dark"]) .research-articles {
    --description-accent: #d6a387;
    --description-bg: rgba(214, 163, 135, 0.065);
  }

  .research-article-list { list-style: none; }

  .research-article-toggle {
    position: relative;
    min-width: 0;
    max-width: 100%;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 3px;
    background: transparent;
    color: inherit;
    font: inherit;
    text-align: left;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .research-article-toggle:hover { color: var(--link); }
